.TH GETNETBYNAME_R 3
.SH NAME
getnetbyname_r, getnetbyaddr_r, getnetent_r \- reentrant network database lookups
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <netdb.h>
.PP
.BI "int getnetbyname_r(const char *" name ", struct netent *" ret ,
.BI "char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct netent **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int getnetbyaddr_r(uint32_t " net ", int " type ", struct netent *" ret ,
.BI "char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct netent **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int getnetent_r(struct netent *" ret ", char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ,
.BI "struct netent **" result ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are the reentrant equivalents of
.BR getnetbyname (3),
.BR getnetbyaddr (3)
and
.BR getnetent (3).
The matching
.I /etc/networks
entry is copied into the caller-supplied
.I ret
structure and scratch buffer
.IR buf
(length
.IR buflen );
.I *result
points at
.I ret
on success or is NULL when no entry matches.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success, or ERANGE if
.I buf
is too small.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ERANGE
.I buf
was too small to hold the result.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getnetent (3),
.BR getprotobyname_r (3),
.BR gethostbyname_r (3)
.SH STANDARDS
GNU extension.
